Linux commands for Devops Engineer
----------------------------------
ls - list
mkdir - make directory
cd - change to directory
touch - create empty file 
nano - enter some text or edit the file, create a new file 
cat - show the file 
rm [filename] - remove the file or delete 
rm * - everything inside that directory will be deleted
cd .. - back to one directory
cd ../ - two steps back to the directory
cd - back to home directory
mkdir [file name] && cd [file name]
rmdir [dir name ] - remove directory [make sure it is empty]
rm -r [dir name] - even it is had some files
man rm or any command name - gives the manual of that command
cp [file name] [the file or directory to copy] -copy the file
mv [file name] [the file or directory to copy] - move the file
mv [file name ] [~/[home folder name ]  - move file to home dir
mv - used for move as well as rename the file
sudo apt update & upgrade
sudo apt purge - for deleting the package
ssh [key name] ubuntu@[instance ip] - for remote login into the EC2 instance 
mkdir [dirname] && touch [dir name]/[file name] - it will create a directory as well as create new file inside the directory
exit - exit from the instance
history - to check all the previous runned commands
pwd - present working directory [to check the current working directory]
we can remove the entire path by using the command rm [that dir]
whoami - see the root user
[name] --version - version of the package
which docker - tocheck where it is installed or located
date - current date 
vi [filename] - create and edit file
to write something - press 'i' in keyboard
exit the editor - press escape button 
:wq - save and exit
qa! - exit without saving
ping - to check connection is established or not [network cmd]
ping google.com 
ip addr - to check the ip address
nslookup google.com - give name, ip address 
curl google.com - to get all the thing which appear on website in html format
